{"availability":"available","full":"sergeyprokudin/dpf","name":"dpf","description":"Dynamic Point Fields: Towards Efficient and Scalable Dynamic Surface Representations (ICCV 2023)","category":"Other","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":90,"forks":4,"created":"2023-04-30T13:00:07Z","updated":"2024-04-30T14:30:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://colab.research.google.com/github//sergeyprokudin/dpf/blob/main/colab_notebooks/Single_Scan_Animation.ipynb","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.518Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.518Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.518Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.518Z","stars":90,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is an official code for the paper \"Dynamic Point Fields\" (ICCV 2023 Oral).","In a nutshell: we propose to model dynamic surfaces with a point-based model, where the motion of a point over time is represented by an implicit deformation field. Working directly with points (rather than SDFs) allows us to easily incorporate various well-known deformation constraints, e.g. as-isometric-as-possible (AIAP). We showcase the usefulness of this approach for creating animatable avatars in complex clothing:","Please see Section 4.3 of the paper for more details."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sergeyprokudin/dpf/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9ca3a3b3a96c6ea102b05b7c2bf44b86a3382092f4a0de2e3710bbb42e47c583","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.627Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.627Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is an official code for the paper \"Dynamic Point Fields\" (ICCV 2023 Oral).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sergeyprokudin/dpf/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9ca3a3b3a96c6ea102b05b7c2bf44b86a3382092f4a0de2e3710bbb42e47c583","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sergeyprokudin/dpf/